{"hw":"μηδέ","html":"<div class=\"lex-entry\"><h4 class=\"lex-hw gk\">μηδέ</h4><span class=\"lex-orth gk\">μηδέ</span>, (<span class=\"lex-etym gk\">μή, δέ</span>) neg. Particle (cf. <span class=\"gk\">οὐδέ</span>): <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"1\"><span class=\"lex-n\">A</span> as Conj., <b class=\"lex-tr\">and not</b> (<span class=\"lex-gram\"> <span class=\"lex-gram\">Ep.</span> </span> also, <b class=\"lex-tr\">but not), nor</b>, connecting two whole clauses, used with the same constructions as <span class=\"gk\">μή, μή τι σὺ ταῦτα.. διείρεο μηδὲ μετάλλα</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Il.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1.550</span> </span>, etc.: without a neg. preceding, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">4.302</span> </span>, etc.; <span class=\"gk\">τεκνοῦσθαι, μηδ' ἄπαιδα θνῄσκειν</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">A.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ag.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">754</span> </span> (lyr.), cf. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Eu.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">714</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Supp.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">409</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">ὕδατος, μελίσσης, μηδὲ προσφέρειν μέθυ</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">S.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">OC</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">481</span> </span>, cf. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Th.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">7.77</span> </span>. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"3\"><span class=\"lex-n\">2</span> in <span class=\"gk\">μηδέ.. μηδέ</span>.. the first <span class=\"gk\">μ.</span> may belong to <span class=\"gk\">μηδέ</span> A, e.g. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Il.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">4.303</span> </span> sq., or to <span class=\"gk\">μηδέ</span> B, e.g. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pl.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">R.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">391c</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">μήτε.. μηδέ</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pi.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">I.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">2.45</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pl.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Prt.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">327d</span> </span>; but <span class=\"gk\">μήτε</span> cannot follow <span class=\"gk\">μηδέ</span>:—for <span class=\"gk\">μηδέ</span> after <span class=\"gk\">οὐδέ</span>, v. οὐ <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">A.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">11.3</span> </span>. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"1\"><span class=\"lex-n\">B</span> as <span class=\"lex-gram\">Adv.</span>, joined with a single word or phrase, <b class=\"lex-tr\">not even, not either</b>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Il.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">21.375</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Od.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">4.710</span> </span>, etc.; repeated emphatically, <span class=\"gk\">μηδ' ὅντινα γαστέρι μήτηρ κοῦρον ἐόντα φέροι μηδ' ὃς φύγοι</span> let <b class=\"lex-tr\">not</b> the babe unborn —<b class=\"lex-tr\">no let not even</b> it escape, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Il.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">6.58</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">τὸ μήποτ' αὖθις μηδ' ἀναστῆναι</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">A.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ag.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">569</span> </span>:—for <span class=\"gk\">μηδέ τι</span> v. μήτις.</div></div>"}